ll keep thee;¦layout§quote_2‚¤textÙ/And when thou awakest, it shall talk with thee.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ4For the commandment is a lamp; and the law is light;¦layout ‚¤textÙ0And reproofs of instruction are the way of life:¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ!To keep thee from the evil woman,¦layout ‚¤textÙ3From the flattery of the tongue of a strange woman.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ)Lust not after her beauty in thine heart;¦layout ‚¤textÙ+Neither let her take thee with her eyelids.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙEFor by means of a whorish woman a man is brought to a piece of bread:¦layout ‚¤textÙ3And the adulteress will hunt for the precious life.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ!Can a man take fire in his bosom,¦layout ‚¤text¾And his clothes not be burned?¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textºCan one go upon hot coals,¦layout ‚¤text»And his feet not be burned?¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ,So he that goeth in to his neighbour's wife;¦layout ‚¤textÙ-Whosoever toucheth her shall not be innocent.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ'Men do not despise a thief, if he steal¦layout ‚¤textÙ&To satisfy his soul when he is hungry;¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ/But if he be found, he shall restore sevenfold;¦layout ‚¤textÙ-He shall give all the substance of his house.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verse ªlast_verse#¦verses”„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙABut whoso committeth adultery with a woman lacketh understanding:¦layout ‚¤textÙ)He that doeth it destroyeth his own soul.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ#A wound and dishonour shall he get;¦layout ‚¤textÙ)And his reproach shall not be wiped away.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ"For jealousy is the rage of a man:¦layout ‚¤textÙ4Therefore he will not spare in the day of vengeance.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤text¾He will not regard any ransom;¦layout ‚¤textÙ<Neither will he rest content, though thou givest many gifts.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse#